-- Employment Act 1968 (Singapore) and the Employment (Retrenchment Reporting) Notification 2019 -- LAYER 1,
-- THE DUTIES AS REGULATIVE RULES.  Part ea2.
-- Source text: inputs/EmA1968.txt and inputs/EmA1968-S200-2019.txt (converter renderings, not the official texts).
--
-- Notes for the reader.
--   * Each duty with a time limit is written as a regulative rule (PARTY ... MUST ... WITHIN ... LEST BREACH BY ... BECAUSE ...).
--     The unit of WITHIN is the DAY.  The clock starts at 0 on the day the duty arises; the number of days allowed is worked out
--     by the decision functions of the module of that section, so the two forms agree.
--   * A prohibition whose bearer the text names (ss 68(1), 81, 105(4), 106) is derived from the answer of the decision function:
--     the rule is the prohibition only where that answer is JUST FALSE (the N2 ruling).  Where the bearer is not named
--     (ss 69, 73, 102(1), 102(3), 105B) no SHANT is written and the Jural relations table says so.
--   * A deontic value cannot be compared with EQUALS in an #ASSERT on the main binary; each rule is run with #TRACE and
--     read by eye (NOTES.md, What the main binary does not accept).  The decision function beside each rule has the #ASSERTs.
--   * `WAIT UNTIL` is not a name on the main binary used here, so a missed deadline is shown by a late act.

§ `Duties -- prohibitions derived from a flat negative`

DECLARE `s 68(1) Person who must not employ a child` IS ONE OF
    `s 68(1) a person`

DECLARE `s 68(1) Act` IS ONE OF
    `s 68(1) employs a child`

-- s 68(1): "A person must not employ a child in an industrial or a non-industrial undertaking except as provided for in
-- subsections (2) and (3)."
-- src:2648 | 68.—(1) A person must not employ a child in an industrial or a
-- src:2649 | non‑industrial undertaking except as provided for in subsections (2)
-- src:2650 | and (3).
@ref s 68(1) (src:2648-2650)
GIVEN `the answer of s 68(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 68(1) the prohibition on employing a child` MEANS
    IF `the answer of s 68(1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN (PARTY `s 68(1) a person` SHANT `s 68(1) employs a child`
          LEST BREACH BY `s 68(1) a person` BECAUSE "a person employed a child in an undertaking, which section 68(1) forbids except as provided for in subsections (2) and (3)")
    ELSE FULFILLED

#TRACE `s 68(1) the prohibition on employing a child` (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 68(1) a person` DOES `s 68(1) employs a child` AT 3

-- the answer is not that the person may not: the rule does not bite
#TRACE `s 68(1) the prohibition on employing a child` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 68(1) a person` DOES `s 68(1) employs a child` AT 3

#TRACE `s 68(1) the prohibition on employing a child` NOTHING AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 68(1) a person` DOES `s 68(1) employs a child` AT 3

DECLARE `s 81 Person who must not give notice` IS ONE OF
    `s 81 her employer`

DECLARE `s 81 Act` IS ONE OF
    `s 81 gives her notice of dismissal during her absence or so that the notice will expire during it`

-- s 81: "it is not lawful for her employer to give her notice of dismissal during her absence or on such a day that the notice
-- will expire during her absence."
-- src:2996 | 81. Without affecting sections 84 and 84A, when a female
-- src:2997 | employee absents herself from work in accordance with the
-- src:2998 | provisions of this Part it is not lawful for her employer to give her
-- src:2999 | notice of dismissal during her absence or on such a day that the notice
-- src:3000 | will expire during her absence.
@ref s 81 (src:2996-3000)
GIVEN `the answer of s 81` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 81 the prohibition on giving her notice of dismissal` MEANS
    IF `the answer of s 81` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN (PARTY `s 81 her employer` SHANT `s 81 gives her notice of dismissal during her absence or so that the notice will expire during it`
          LEST BREACH BY `s 81 her employer` BECAUSE "her employer gave her notice of dismissal during her absence or on such a day that the notice will expire during her absence")
    ELSE FULFILLED

#TRACE `s 81 the prohibition on giving her notice of dismissal` (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 81 her employer` DOES `s 81 gives her notice of dismissal during her absence or so that the notice will expire during it` AT 12

#TRACE `s 81 the prohibition on giving her notice of dismissal` NOTHING AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 81 her employer` DOES `s 81 gives her notice of dismissal during her absence or so that the notice will expire during it` AT 12

DECLARE `s 105(4) Person who must not detain` IS ONE OF
    `s 105(4) an inspecting officer`

DECLARE `s 105(4) Act` IS ONE OF
    `s 105(4) detains a person arrested without warrant for longer than is allowed`

-- s 105(4): "An inspecting officer must not detain in custody a person arrested without warrant for longer than is reasonable in
-- the circumstances, and the period must not exceed 48 hours exclusive of the time necessary for the journey".
-- src:4253 | (4) An inspecting officer must not detain in custody a person
-- src:4254 | arrested without warrant for longer than is reasonable in the
-- src:4255 | circumstances, and the period must not exceed 48 hours exclusive
-- src:4260 | of the time necessary for the journey from the place of arrest to the
-- src:4261 | Magistrate’s Court.
@ref s 105(4) (src:4253-4261)
GIVEN `the answer of s 105(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105(4) the prohibition on detaining the person in custody` MEANS
    IF `the answer of s 105(4)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN (PARTY `s 105(4) an inspecting officer` SHANT `s 105(4) detains a person arrested without warrant for longer than is allowed`
          LEST BREACH BY `s 105(4) an inspecting officer` BECAUSE "an inspecting officer detained a person arrested without warrant for longer than is reasonable in the circumstances or for more than 48 hours")
    ELSE FULFILLED

#TRACE `s 105(4) the prohibition on detaining the person in custody` (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 105(4) an inspecting officer` DOES `s 105(4) detains a person arrested without warrant for longer than is allowed` AT 49

#TRACE `s 105(4) the prohibition on detaining the person in custody` NOTHING AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 105(4) an inspecting officer` DOES `s 105(4) detains a person arrested without warrant for longer than is allowed` AT 49

DECLARE `s 106 Person who must not reveal` IS ONE OF
    `s 106 a person`

DECLARE `s 106 Act` IS ONE OF
    `s 106 reveals a manufacturing or commercial secret that came to the person's knowledge as an inspecting officer`

-- s 106: "A person must not, except in the performance of his or her duties, reveal any manufacturing or commercial secrets which
-- may at any time come to his or her knowledge in the course of his or her duty as an inspecting officer."
-- src:4357 | 106. A person must not, except in the performance of his or her
-- src:4358 | duties, reveal any manufacturing or commercial secrets which may at
-- src:4359 | any time come to his or her knowledge in the course of his or her duty
-- src:4360 | as an inspecting officer.
-- src:4362 | Disposal of documents, articles, etc.
@ref s 106 (src:4357-4362)
GIVEN `the answer of s 106` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 106 the prohibition on revealing a manufacturing or commercial secret` MEANS
    IF `the answer of s 106` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN (PARTY `s 106 a person` SHANT `s 106 reveals a manufacturing or commercial secret that came to the person's knowledge as an inspecting officer`
          LEST BREACH BY `s 106 a person` BECAUSE "a person revealed a manufacturing or commercial secret that came to the person's knowledge in the course of his or her duty as an inspecting officer, other than in the performance of his or her duties")
    ELSE FULFILLED

#TRACE `s 106 the prohibition on revealing a manufacturing or commercial secret` (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 106 a person` DOES `s 106 reveals a manufacturing or commercial secret that came to the person's knowledge as an inspecting officer` AT 5

#TRACE `s 106 the prohibition on revealing a manufacturing or commercial secret` NOTHING AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 106 a person` DOES `s 106 reveals a manufacturing or commercial secret that came to the person's knowledge as an inspecting officer` AT 5

§ `Duties -- duties with a time limit`

DECLARE `s 78(1) Person who pays` IS ONE OF
    `s 78(1) the employer`

DECLARE `s 78(1) Act` IS ONE OF
    `s 78(1) pays the first instalment`
    `s 78(1) pays the second instalment`

-- s 78(1): the payment is in 2 instalments, "the first instalment ... to be paid within 7 days from the date of confinement and
-- the second instalment ... within 7 days from the end of that period".  The clock starts at 0 on the day of confinement; the days
-- allowed are worked out by `s 78(1) the last day for paying the first instalment` and `... the second instalment`.
-- src:2929 | 78.—(1) In the case of a female employee who is a daily‑rated
-- src:2930 | employee, the payment referred to in section 76 must be paid in
-- src:2931 | 2 instalments, the first for the period up to and including the day of
-- src:2936 | confinement, to be paid within 7 days from the date of confinement,
-- src:2937 | and the second, for the period after confinement, to be paid within
-- src:2938 | 7 days from the end of that period.
@ref s 78(1) (src:2929-2938)
GIVEN `the days allowed for the first instalment` IS A NUMBER
      `the days allowed for the second instalment` IS A NUMBER
`s 78(1) the duty to pay the payment in 2 instalments` MEANS
    (PARTY `s 78(1) the employer` MUST `s 78(1) pays the first instalment` WITHIN `the days allowed for the first instalment`
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY `s 78(1) the employer` BECAUSE "the first instalment was not paid within 7 days from the date of confinement")
    RAND
    (PARTY `s 78(1) the employer` MUST `s 78(1) pays the second instalment` WITHIN `the days allowed for the second instalment`
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY `s 78(1) the employer` BECAUSE "the second instalment was not paid within 7 days from the end of the benefit period")

-- Confinement on Wednesday 10 June 2026; first instalment due Wednesday 17 June (7 days); the benefit period (56 days from 13 May)
-- ends Tuesday 7 July; second instalment due Tuesday 14 July (34 days after 10 June).
#TRACE `s 78(1) the duty to pay the payment in 2 instalments` 7 34 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 78(1) the employer` DOES `s 78(1) pays the first instalment` AT 7
    PARTY `s 78(1) the employer` DOES `s 78(1) pays the second instalment` AT 34

#TRACE `s 78(1) the duty to pay the payment in 2 instalments` 7 34 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 78(1) the employer` DOES `s 78(1) pays the first instalment` AT 8
    PARTY `s 78(1) the employer` DOES `s 78(1) pays the second instalment` AT 34

#TRACE `s 78(1) the duty to pay the payment in 2 instalments` 7 34 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 78(1) the employer` DOES `s 78(1) pays the first instalment` AT 7
    PARTY `s 78(1) the employer` DOES `s 78(1) pays the second instalment` AT 35

DECLARE `s 80(1) Person who gives notice` IS ONE OF
    `s 80(1) the female employee`

DECLARE `s 80(1) Act` IS ONE OF
    `s 80(1) gives her employer notice of the date she intends to begin absenting herself`

-- s 80(1): "A female employee must, at least one week before absenting herself from work in accordance with section 76, give
-- notice to her employer specifying the date on which she intends to commence absenting herself from work."  The clock starts at 0
-- today; the days allowed are the days from today to 7 days before the first day of her absence.
-- src:2970 | 80.—(1) A female employee must, at least one week before
-- src:2971 | absenting herself from work in accordance with section 76, give
-- src:2972 | notice to her employer specifying the date on which she intends to
-- src:2973 | commence absenting herself from work.
@ref s 80(1) (src:2970-2973)
GIVEN `the days from today until one week before the first day of the absence` IS A NUMBER
`s 80(1) the duty to give notice` MEANS
    PARTY `s 80(1) the female employee` MUST `s 80(1) gives her employer notice of the date she intends to begin absenting herself`
    WITHIN `the days from today until one week before the first day of the absence`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 80(1) the female employee` BECAUSE "she did not give her employer notice at least one week before absenting herself"

-- absence to begin in 20 days: the notice is due within 13 days
#TRACE `s 80(1) the duty to give notice` 13 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 80(1) the female employee` DOES `s 80(1) gives her employer notice of the date she intends to begin absenting herself` AT 13

#TRACE `s 80(1) the duty to give notice` 13 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 80(1) the female employee` DOES `s 80(1) gives her employer notice of the date she intends to begin absenting herself` AT 14

DECLARE `s 87A(4) Person who grants or takes the leave` IS ONE OF
    `s 87A(4) the employer`
    `s 87A(4) the employee`

DECLARE `s 87A(4) Act` IS ONE OF
    `s 87A(4) grants the childcare leave`
    `s 87A(4) takes the childcare leave`

-- s 87A(4): "An employer must grant, and an employee who is entitled to childcare leave must take, the entitlement of childcare
-- leave of 2 days for a relevant period not later than the last day of that relevant period".  The clock starts at 0 today.
-- src:3275 | (4) An employer must grant, and an employee who is entitled to
-- src:3276 | childcare leave must take, the entitlement of childcare leave of 2 days
-- src:3277 | for a relevant period not later than the last day of that relevant period,
-- src:3278 | and any employee who fails to take that leave by that day —
-- src:3280 | (a) thereupon ceases to be entitled to that leave; and
-- src:3282 | (b) is not entitled to any payment in lieu thereof.
@ref s 87A(4) (src:3275-3282)
GIVEN `the days from today until the last day of the relevant period` IS A NUMBER
`s 87A(4) the duty to grant and to take the childcare leave` MEANS
    (PARTY `s 87A(4) the employer` MUST `s 87A(4) grants the childcare leave` WITHIN `the days from today until the last day of the relevant period`
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY `s 87A(4) the employer` BECAUSE "the employer did not grant the childcare leave by the last day of the relevant period")
    RAND
    (PARTY `s 87A(4) the employee` MUST `s 87A(4) takes the childcare leave` WITHIN `the days from today until the last day of the relevant period`
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY `s 87A(4) the employee` BECAUSE "the employee did not take the childcare leave by the last day of the relevant period, and so ceases to be entitled to it and to any payment in lieu")

#TRACE `s 87A(4) the duty to grant and to take the childcare leave` 100 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 87A(4) the employer` DOES `s 87A(4) grants the childcare leave` AT 10
    PARTY `s 87A(4) the employee` DOES `s 87A(4) takes the childcare leave` AT 100

#TRACE `s 87A(4) the duty to grant and to take the childcare leave` 100 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 87A(4) the employer` DOES `s 87A(4) grants the childcare leave` AT 10
    PARTY `s 87A(4) the employee` DOES `s 87A(4) takes the childcare leave` AT 101

DECLARE `s 88A(6) Person who grants or takes the leave` IS ONE OF
    `s 88A(6) the employer`
    `s 88A(6) the employee`

DECLARE `s 88A(6) Act` IS ONE OF
    `s 88A(6) grants the paid annual leave`
    `s 88A(6) takes the paid annual leave`

-- s 88A(6)(a): for a workman mentioned in s 35(a) or an employee to whom Part 4 applies by virtue of s 35(b), "the employer must
-- grant, and the employee must take, the employee's paid annual leave not later than 12 months after the end of every 12 months of
-- continuous service".  The clock starts at 0 today; the answers of s 35(a) and (b) decide whether the duty is there at all.
-- src:3540 | (6) In the case of an employee to whom Part 4 applies by virtue of
-- src:3541 | section 35(b) or who is a workman mentioned in section 35(a) —
-- src:3543 | (a) the employer must grant, and the employee must take, the
-- src:3544 | employee’s paid annual leave not later than 12 months after
-- src:3545 | the end of every 12 months of continuous service; and
@ref s 88A(6)(a) (src:3540-3545)
GIVEN `the answer of s 35(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 35(b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the days from today until the last day for taking the paid annual leave` IS A NUMBER
`s 88A(6)(a) the duty to grant and to take the paid annual leave` MEANS
    IF `the answer of s 35(a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the answer of s 35(b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN ((PARTY `s 88A(6) the employer` MUST `s 88A(6) grants the paid annual leave` WITHIN `the days from today until the last day for taking the paid annual leave`
              HENCE FULFILLED
              LEST BREACH BY `s 88A(6) the employer` BECAUSE "the employer did not grant the paid annual leave not later than 12 months after the end of the 12 months of continuous service")
          RAND
          (PARTY `s 88A(6) the employee` MUST `s 88A(6) takes the paid annual leave` WITHIN `the days from today until the last day for taking the paid annual leave`
              HENCE FULFILLED
              LEST BREACH BY `s 88A(6) the employee` BECAUSE "the employee did not take the paid annual leave not later than 12 months after the end of the 12 months of continuous service, and so ceases to be entitled to it"))
    ELSE FULFILLED

#TRACE `s 88A(6)(a) the duty to grant and to take the paid annual leave` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) 30 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 88A(6) the employer` DOES `s 88A(6) grants the paid annual leave` AT 5
    PARTY `s 88A(6) the employee` DOES `s 88A(6) takes the paid annual leave` AT 30

#TRACE `s 88A(6)(a) the duty to grant and to take the paid annual leave` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) 30 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 88A(6) the employer` DOES `s 88A(6) grants the paid annual leave` AT 5
    PARTY `s 88A(6) the employee` DOES `s 88A(6) takes the paid annual leave` AT 31

DECLARE `s 95A(2) Person who gives the record` IS ONE OF
    `s 95A(2) the employer`

DECLARE `s 95A(2) Act` IS ONE OF
    `s 95A(2) gives the employee a written record of the key employment terms`

-- s 95A(2): "An employer must give each employee of the employer a written record of the key employment terms of the employee not
-- later than 14 days after the day that the employee starts employment".  The clock starts at 0 on the day the employee starts.
-- src:3864 | (2) An employer must give each employee of the employer a
-- src:3865 | written record of the key employment terms of the employee not later
-- src:3866 | than 14 days after the day that the employee starts employment with
-- src:3867 | the employer, or within such other period as may be prescribed in
-- src:3868 | substitution.
@ref s 95A(2) (src:3864-3868)
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
`s 95A(2) the duty to give the written record` MEANS
    PARTY `s 95A(2) the employer` MUST `s 95A(2) gives the employee a written record of the key employment terms`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 95A(2) the employer` BECAUSE "the employer did not give the employee a written record of the key employment terms not later than 14 days after the day the employee started employment"

-- Employee starts Monday 4 May 2026; the last day is Monday 18 May: 14 days.
#TRACE `s 95A(2) the duty to give the written record` 14 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 95A(2) the employer` DOES `s 95A(2) gives the employee a written record of the key employment terms` AT 14

#TRACE `s 95A(2) the duty to give the written record` 14 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 95A(2) the employer` DOES `s 95A(2) gives the employee a written record of the key employment terms` AT 15

DECLARE `S 200/2019 para 4 Person who gives the report` IS ONE OF
    `S 200/2019 para 4 the employer`

DECLARE `S 200/2019 para 4 Act` IS ONE OF
    `S 200/2019 para 4 gives the Commissioner the retrenchment report`

-- Notification para 4: "Every retrenchment report must be given to the Commissioner not later than 5 working days after the day that
-- the employer gives the notice of retrenchment".  The clock starts at 0 on the day the notice is given; the days allowed are worked
-- out by `S 200/2019 para 4 the last day for giving the retrenchment report`.
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:62 | 4. Every retrenchment report must be given to the Commissioner
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:63 | not later than 5 working days after the day that the employer gives the
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:64 | notice of retrenchment mentioned in paragraph 3.
@ref para 4 (src:EmA1968-S200-2019:62-64)
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
`S 200/2019 para 4 the duty to give the retrenchment report` MEANS
    PARTY `S 200/2019 para 4 the employer` MUST `S 200/2019 para 4 gives the Commissioner the retrenchment report`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `S 200/2019 para 4 the employer` BECAUSE "the employer did not give the Commissioner the retrenchment report not later than 5 working days after the day it gave the notice of retrenchment"

-- Notice given Wednesday 4 November 2026; the 5th working day after is Wednesday 11 November: 7 days.
#TRACE `S 200/2019 para 4 the duty to give the retrenchment report` 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `S 200/2019 para 4 the employer` DOES `S 200/2019 para 4 gives the Commissioner the retrenchment report` AT 7

#TRACE `S 200/2019 para 4 the duty to give the retrenchment report` 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `S 200/2019 para 4 the employer` DOES `S 200/2019 para 4 gives the Commissioner the retrenchment report` AT 8

-- The decision functions agree with the traces: the days allowed come from the layer-1 modules, and the same date arithmetic is
-- asserted there.  Here the two forms are tied together once.
GIVEN `the day the employee starts employment` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 95A(2) the days allowed for giving the written record` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 95A(2) the last day for giving the written record of the key employment terms` `the day the employee starts employment` NOTHING `the public holidays` FALSE
    WHEN JUST last THEN JUST (last MINUS `the day the employee starts employment`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a contrary intention or a missing last day leaves no count of days
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 95A(2) the days allowed for giving the written record` (Date 4 5 2026) EMPTY EQUALS JUST 14
#ASSERT `s 95A(2) the days allowed for giving the written record` (Date 3 5 2026) EMPTY EQUALS JUST 15
#ASSERT `s 95A(2) the days allowed for giving the written record` (Date 4 5 2026) (LIST Date 18 5 2026) EQUALS JUST 15

GIVEN `the day the employer gave the notice of retrenchment` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`S 200/2019 para 4 the days allowed for giving the retrenchment report` MEANS
    `S 200/2019 para 4 the last day for giving the retrenchment report` `the day the employer gave the notice of retrenchment` `the public holidays` MINUS `the day the employer gave the notice of retrenchment`

#ASSERT `S 200/2019 para 4 the days allowed for giving the retrenchment report` (Date 4 11 2026) EMPTY EQUALS 7
#ASSERT `S 200/2019 para 4 the days allowed for giving the retrenchment report` (Date 6 11 2026) EMPTY EQUALS 7
#ASSERT `S 200/2019 para 4 the days allowed for giving the retrenchment report` (Date 4 11 2026) (LIST Date 9 11 2026) EQUALS 8

GIVEN `the day of the confinement` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the benefit period` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 78(1) the days allowed for the second instalment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 78(1) the last day for paying the second instalment` `the last day of the benefit period` `the public holidays`
    WHEN JUST last THEN JUST (last MINUS `the day of the confinement`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the last day for the second instalment is not given
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

GIVEN `the day of the confinement` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 78(1) the days allowed for the first instalment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 78(1) the last day for paying the first instalment` `the day of the confinement` `the public holidays`
    WHEN JUST last THEN JUST (last MINUS `the day of the confinement`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the last day for the first instalment is not given
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 78(1) the days allowed for the first instalment` (Date 10 6 2026) EMPTY EQUALS JUST 7
#ASSERT `s 78(1) the days allowed for the first instalment` (Date 7 6 2026) EMPTY EQUALS JUST 8
#ASSERT `s 78(1) the days allowed for the second instalment` (Date 10 6 2026) (Date 7 7 2026) EMPTY EQUALS JUST 34

-- The days allowed on the other duties, worked out by decision functions beside the rules (the tests are in ea2-tests-duties.l4).
GIVEN `today` IS A DATE
      `the first day she absents herself from work` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 80(1) the days from today until the last day for giving the notice` MEANS
    (`the first day she absents herself from work` MINUS `today`) MINUS 7

GIVEN `today` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the relevant period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 87A(4) the days from today until the last day of the relevant period` MEANS
    `the last day of the relevant period` MINUS `today`

GIVEN `today` IS A DATE
      `the answer of s 35(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 35(b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the day the 12 months of continuous service ended` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 88A(6)(a) the days from today until the last day for taking the paid annual leave` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 88A(6)(a) the last day for taking the paid annual leave` `the answer of s 35(a)` `the answer of s 35(b)` `the day the 12 months of continuous service ended`
    WHEN JUST last THEN JUST (last MINUS `today`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): neither limb of the duty is shown to apply, so no last day is fixed
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
